<h1>Hausdorff distance</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A measure of the resemblance of two (fixed) sets of geometric points P and Q, defined as H(P,Q)=max{max<sub>a&isin; P</sub> min<sub>b&isin; Q</sub> d(a,b), max<sub>a&isin; Q</sub> min<sub>b&isin; P</sub> d(a,b)} where d(&middot;,&middot;) is the distance metric, usually the <a href="euclidndstnc.html"><em>Euclidean distance</em></a>.
</p>


<p>
<em>Note:
Adapted from <a href="../terms.html#AS98">[AS98, page 437]</a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

